commit 9e0d5050db7d00c1ca4050d30b034d2cec5ce7c1
Author: YueGuobin <yueguobin@outlook.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 14 21:52:34 2026 +0800

    feat: concurrent kernel captures, one per interface
    
    uBridge's capture module now serves one AF_PACKET capture per interface,
    any number per process, and `capture stop_kernel` takes the interface it
    stops — this rides that (breaking, paired-binary) protocol change.
    
    The server-side single-slot tracker (_kernel_capture_ifc with its
    reserve/release/owned_by helpers) is gone: same-port duplicates were
    already refused by the NIO capturing flag, uBridge answers EALREADY on a
    same-interface duplicate, and per-interface stops removed the process-
    wide stop the ownership gating guarded against.
    
    The docker e2e drives ten concurrent captures on one node's uBridge and
    asserts a per-interface stop freezes exactly the stopped half while the
    live half keeps recording.

